{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440557-first-2nd-edition-chronicle","id":440557,"title":"First 2nd Edition Chronicle.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T16:23:17-07:00","id":440557,"title":"First 2nd Edition Chronicle.","content":"I'm running my first Werewolf: The Forsaken chronicle ever tonight, and I am looking for some ideas to run a basic, traditionally themed werewolf session.<br /> What are some things that werewolves regularly have to deal with? What is a good launching pad for a chronicle?<br /> I know very little about 1st edition, but I've read most of The Idigam Chronicles, and have garnered most of my information from it. The feel and mood of 2nd edition seems quite different from the first, and I want to try to capture that. &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot;.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions on plot hooks I could run or tips for a new Forsaken storyteller? Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1310,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","user":"Samare","date":".  Grammar and stuff. 03-13-2015, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:52:31-07:00","id":440634,"title":"","content":"My first chronicle starts in April and I'm running it to focus on a Protectorate tearing itself apart to demonstrate the savagry of Rage and the ultimate failing of reason to overcome it. It's designed to be a tragety, not a morality tale.<br /> <br /> For plot hooks use pack generation. Players are going to create wolfblooded and human characters. Do horrifying things to their families. Possession, Host invasion, and abduction by the Pure are all powerful motivations for the pack to declare a hunt.<br /> <br /> Find out what your pack cares about and then attack it at it's core. Say the pack runs a bar to keep themselves stable. A newer, better bar opens up the road very suddenly. Is it urbanization spirits motivating construction? Is it a bitter enemy of the pack striking at them wth a cat's paw? Or maybe the pack is an extended family. Have one of the family members start dating someone the rest don't approve of, someone that they know is bad news.<br /> <br /> Push the feeling of constant assault on the player's lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:35:08-07:00","id":440666,"title":"","content":"Probably the most simple story would be about finding and claiming a territory, which usually involves dealing with antagonists who are in the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:05:04-07:00","id":440702,"title":"","content":"Get the demo from the white wolf archive, it's free and will give plenty of story tellingn examples. Also the werewolf the apocalypse story tellers guide, revised edition.<br /> <br /> Best I can tell ya is work with what you know best. Emphasize werewolf as a primal hunter. You're a beast, you feel it. Express the new alien nature. How mankind feels different now. How pointless jobs feel, how stupid it is to pay for meat.<br /> <br /> Find and read the short story 'wereman' by i think it's Les Daniels. Actually find the mammoth book of wolf men and flip through that. Great damn book and available on kindle. Features authors like clive barker and Neil gaiman, as well as the story I suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:53:10-07:00","id":441300,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't suggest the Werewolf the Apocalypse guide, if only because it's a very different kind of game. Look at the Storyteller Chapter in the Forsaken Second Edition corebook instead; it has much of what you will need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:05:26-07:00","id":441530,"title":"","content":"I respectfully disagree. While it is a different game line, there is some stuff in there, specifically about story telling a monster that is universal to werewolves. You could cut the majority of the apocalypse content from it and still come out with a wealth of good advice. Things often forgotten or overlooked for word count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}